ops/data/

# Local tooling: a symlink to /opt/scripts/originfacts on the build host.
# Absolute and machine-specific, so it dangles anywhere else — on Vercel it
# made `next build` fail with ENOENT stat /vercel/path0/scripts.
scripts

# Editor swap files
.*.swp

# Stage 1 capture archive — large, and reproducible by re-running the fetcher.
# Excluded per-entry, not as a directory: git cannot re-include a file inside
# an excluded directory, so `data/captures/` would have made the negation below
# silently inert.
data/captures/*
# ...except the reachability report. It is small, it is the artifact we re-run
# and diff against, and a capture archive is not the same kind of thing as a
# measurement of whether capturing is possible at all.
!data/captures/reachability.json
# Manual captures are tracked in full, bytes included.
#
# An automated capture is reproducible — re-run the fetcher and you get it back.
# A manual one is not: nobody can re-run a person saving a page from a browser
# they were sitting at, on a date that has passed, from a carrier that refuses
# this host. The bytes ARE the evidence, so they are versioned.
#
# Gotcha, hit twice while writing these rules: git will not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation for a file inside one is silently inert.
# That is why the parent is `data/captures/*` rather than `data/captures/`, and
# why both the directory and its children are re-included below. Verify any
# change here with `git check-ignore -v`, not by reading it.
!data/captures/manual/
!data/captures/manual/**
# ...but not the extraction output that lands beside them. candidates.json is
# derived from the tracked bytes by a tracked script, so it is reproducible in
# the way the HTML is not, and versioning it would dirty the tree on every
# re-extract.
data/captures/manual/**/candidates.json
ops/fetch/node_modules
run/
